Suggested attribution:

  token-spread strict identity register — https://github.com/hangryclaude/token-spread
  187 techniques adjudicated, 67 pass. CC BY 4.0.

Why the register is licensed differently from the code: the code is meant to be
taken and run by anyone, with no strings. The register is a claim about what is
true, and a claim that travels without its source becomes a rumour. Attribution
is not a toll — it is the mechanism by which a corrected entry reaches everyone
who repeated it. This register has already been wrong in public four times and
said so; that only works if the people quoting it can be found again.
